      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i really need some help with my monstera deliciosa. i've been growing it for a while but lately something really strange and kind of unsettling is happening. i'm noticing these dark, almost bruised-looking spots appearing on the leaves, and they seem to be spreading in these very jagged, irregular patterns that don't look like normal leaf decay. it's almost like the plant is being targeted or attacked. i live in seattle so it's pretty damp, but the damage looks so sudden and aggressive, like something is actively working against it. is there any kind of pest or some kind of hidden thing in the soil that could cause this kind of weird, targeted damage? it feels less like a natural decline and more like something is actually \"doing\" this to the plant.",
